WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.750
Now one important thing to remember with

00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:04.110
these two memory layers is that as I

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:05.990
mentioned, they are loaded every

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.390
session. So the Claude.md as well as the

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:11.110
memory.md, every time you open a session

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:13.270
or a chat window with Claude Code, those

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:15.310
are always pre-injected once you start

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:16.990
giving a prompt to Claude Code. And if

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.750
you're curious how many tokens that is

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:20.750
consuming already, you can just type in

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:22.750
/context just like what we did with the

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:24.950
skills before. And under the memory

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:26.990
files, this green layer here, that will

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.470
tell you exactly how big your Claude.md

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:31.910
plus your memory.md is right now in

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:34.070
terms of tokens. So right now with this

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:36.670
8,100 tokens, it is actually quite

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:38.310
healthy. There's not really a rule

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:40.630
around how big or how small your

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:43.070
Claude.md or memory.md is because each

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:44.510
of our work is different. But obviously

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:46.830
if this is already exceeding like 50,000

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:48.230
tokens just from your memory and

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:50.310
Claude.md files, then that might be

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:52.310
worth auditing your files. Just to make

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:53.910
sure that they are not hounding your

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:56.430
tokens, especially if you are on the Pro

00:00:56.440 --> 00:00:58.750
Plan. Because amongst these categories,

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:00.590
the system prompt and the system tools,

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:03.110
that is pre-coded by Anthropic as part

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:04.590
of the Claude Code Harness. So there's

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:06.790
not much that we can do there or change,

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:08.670
but our memory files as well as the

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:11.190
skill descriptions, those are malleable

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:13.230
by the user. And so if you're looking to

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:14.630
manage your tokens a bit better, then

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:16.590
that might be one thing that you want to

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:19.360
just check.
